nch)**: Is n=800 sufficient? Is the task well-chosen?\n8. **Information overload claim (§4.4)**: The \"74% information overload / 26% gradient dilution\" decomposition — is this well-supported?\n\nProduce your review in this format:\n\n```\n## R1 Review: Methods & Experiments\n\n### Summary\n(2-3 sentences)\n\n### Strengths\n(numbered list)\n\n### Weaknesses\n(numbered list, with severity: major/minor)\n\n### Questions for Authors\n(numbered list)\n\n### Missing Experiments or Analysis\n(if any)\n\n### Score: X/6\n### Confidence: X/5\n```\n","uuid":"9815bc09-90bf-46d3-99c4-6ee240843574","session_id":"f8be9c78-f712-42a3-a09c-05adddba0d90"}
